/* 段落记忆 · 词层 4 · 子块 b：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(4,{"sub":"b","par":{"humble":{"tw":[["humility",4],["base",0],["crush",3],["change",2],["proud",1],["quiet",6],["low",5],["hurt",2],["rustic",6],["small",0]],"en":"My grandfather was a humble man who kept a small shop at the base of a low hill. He would never talk about his own skill, and his quiet pride looked more like humility. Once a rich visitor tried to crush him with a rude joke, but he only smiled and went on with his work. That small hurt changed nothing in the way he treated people. He liked plain, rustic things: a wooden chair, a clay cup, a worn mat by the door. Never be proud of what you were given, he told me. He died in the spring, and many strangers came to the little shop to say goodbye.","zh":"我爷爷是个谦和的人，在低矮的山脚下开着一间小铺子。他从不谈自己的手艺，那份安静的自信看上去更像谦逊。有一回，一个有钱的客人想用一句难听的笑话把他压下去，他只是笑笑，接着干手里的活。那点小小的刺伤并没有改变他待人的方式。他喜欢素朴带点土气的东西：一把木椅、一只陶杯、门口一张磨旧了的垫子。他跟我说，别为自己生来就有的东西得意。他在春天去世了，许多素不相识的人都来这间小铺子送他。"},"defy":{"tw":[["defiance",4],["hold",0],["weather",3],["challenge",2],["ignore",6],["dare",0],["brazen",3],["heed",6],["refuse",0]],"en":"An old farmer would defy the weather every spring and plant his seeds in the same week. His neighbours told him to heed the forecast, but he chose to ignore them. As a brazen young man he had taken that dare, and he would not refuse it now. Under a hard sun the dry soil could not hold any water at all. Still he refused to change his plan for the busy season. His quiet defiance made him famous in the valley. When the rain came at last, he only said that the land had passed its challenge.","zh":"有个老农每年春天都要跟天气较劲，总是在同一个星期下种。邻居们劝他看看预报，他却干脆不听。年轻时他胆大，接下了这个赌注，如今也不肯认输。烈日底下，干土根本存不住水。他仍然拒绝为农忙改计划。他这份不声不响的倔强，让他在山谷里出了名。等雨终于落下来，他只说，这块地算是通过了它的考验。"},"exit":{"tw":[["die",0],["fall",3],["move",2],["enter",1],["narrow",6],["issue",0],["abort",3],["play",2],["route",6],["leave",0]],"en":"On the night of the play, the main exit of the hall was blocked by a fallen sign. A narrow side door had to serve the whole crowd. Late visitors would enter through it and then move slowly along the row. The manager feared a fall on the wet steps, and he could not leave the issue alone. If anything worse happened, he would abort the show at once. Someone in the back began to die of laughter at the wrong moment. The route to the street was longer that evening, but nobody was hurt.","zh":"演出那晚，礼堂的主出口被一块倒下的牌子堵住了。一扇窄窄的侧门只好承担全部人流。迟到的观众得从那儿进，再慢慢顺着排往里挪。经理怕大家湿台阶上摔一跤，这件事他放不下。万一再出点更糟的，他打算立刻中止演出。后排有人偏偏在不对的时候笑得直不起腰。那晚出到街上的路绕了些，但没有人受伤。"},"foul":{"tw":[["dirty",5],["stuff",3],["change",2],["fair",1],["ball",6],["nasty",0],["hack",3],["hit",2],["throw",6],["pollute",0]],"en":"The river near the old factory carried a foul smell all summer long. Workers had used it to throw away a grey stuff that nobody could name. The dirty water would pollute every field downstream and change the colour of the grass. A local team played ball on a field close by, and the smell made fair play hard. A nasty fly swarmed over the surface, and a small child began to hack and cough. The town council decided to hit the owners with a heavy fine. In the end the pipes were rebuilt and the smell left for good.","zh":"老工厂旁边那条河，整个夏天都散发着一股臭味。工人们早就习惯往里扔一种谁也说不清的灰色东西。脏水污染了下游每一片田，连草的颜色都变了。当地一支球队就在附近的场地上打球，那股味儿让人根本没法好好比。一只恶心的苍蝇在水面上飞，一个小孩开始咳个不停。镇议会决定重罚厂主。最后管道重新修了，臭味才算彻底散去。"},"hollow":{"tw":[["dig",3],["drive",3],["remove",2],["solid",1],["slab",6],["empty",2],["core",3],["valley",2],["stone",6],["hole",3]],"en":"In the dry valley behind the farm, workers began to dig a deep hole. Their aim was to remove a solid slab of stone for a new road. First they had to drive a long steel bar into the ground. Under the top soil they found a hollow space, the empty core of an old tunnel. Nobody could say who had cut it or when. They covered the hole again with heavy boards and left the stone in the valley. My brother still keeps a small piece of it on his shelf.","zh":"在农场后面那片干谷里，工人们开始挖一个深洞。他们想取出一块坚硬的石板，用来修一条新路。先得把一根长钢钎打进地里。在表层土下面，他们发现了一处空腔，是某条旧隧道的空芯。谁也说不清是谁挖的、什么时候挖的。他们用厚木板把洞重新盖上，把石头留在了谷里。我弟弟至今还在书架上放着其中一小块。"},"evoke":{"tw":[["evocative",4],["raise",0],["draw",3],["cause",2],["conjure",6],["suggest",0],["imitate",6],["stir",0]],"en":"An old song can evoke a whole summer in a second. The smell of rain on hot stone would raise memories I cannot describe. It can draw me back to a narrow street where my friends and I would play until dark. Such a small thing may cause a long and quiet mood, and a few notes can be more evocative than a whole album. My sister likes to imitate the singers of that time, and her voice can conjure the past at once. A single line of music may suggest a face I have half forgotten. It will stir something in me for the rest of the day.","zh":"一首老歌一瞬间就能把人拉回一整个夏天。热石头上落雨的味道，会在我心里勾起说不清的记忆。它能把我带回那条窄街，那时我和朋友一直玩到天黑。这么点小事能让人的情绪沉上一整天，而几个音符，比一整张唱片更能唤起什么。姐姐爱学当年的歌手，她的嗓音一下子就能把过去召回来。一句旋律有时会让我想起一张已经模糊的脸。这一天剩下的时间，心里都会被搅动着。"},"explode":{"tw":[["explosion",4],["burst",0],["erupt",3],["increase",2],["bomb",6],["detonate",0],["dynamite",3],["ignite",6]],"en":"In the old quarry above the valley, workers used dynamite to break the hard stone. The order to detonate was given from behind a thick wall of rock. When the charge began to explode, the explosion sent a low burst of dust over the trees. The sound made the windows of the village shake, and the birds would erupt from the pines. Each blast could ignite small fires in the dry grass. Over the years the work began to increase, and the quarry grew deeper. A bomb in an old war had once made the same noise, one worker said. Nothing about that morning felt safe to me.","zh":"在山谷上方那片旧采石场里，工人们用炸药把坚硬的岩石炸开。点火的指令是从一道厚厚的岩壁后面发出的。炸药一爆，那股冲劲卷起一片尘土，从树顶上漫过去。响声震得村里的窗户直晃，松林里的鸟一下全飞了起来。每次爆破都可能把干草引着。这些年活儿越来越多，石坑也越挖越深。一个工人说，从前打仗时的炸弹也是这个响。那个早上在我眼里一点都不安全。"},"defer":{"tw":[["table",0],["call",3],["delay",2],["withhold",6],["bow",0],["hold",3],["yield",2],["waive",6],["submit",0]],"en":"Because of a heavy storm, the school had to defer the sports day until the next month. The head would table the whole plan and call the parents in the morning. It was better to delay than to risk an accident on the wet field. The office decided to withhold the trophies for another week and to waive the old entry fee for every team. We had to bow to the weather and hold our practice indoors. The team chose to yield the date to a later weekend. In the end we had to submit a new list of events.","zh":"因为一场大风雨，学校只好把运动会推迟到下个月。校长把整个方案先搁起来，第二天早上再打电话通知家长。与其在湿漉漉的场地上冒出事的险，不如往后推。办公室决定把奖杯再压一周，并免掉各队原来的报名费。我们只能向天气低头，把训练改在室内。队里同意把日期让到后面某个周末。最后我们还交了一份新的比赛项目表。"},"deprive":{"tw":[["strip",0],["clean",3],["withhold",2],["enrich",1],["humiliate",6],["impoverish",0],["starve",3],["intimidate",6],["divest",0]],"en":"A report said that the old factory would deprive its workers of rest and fair pay. Bosses would strip them of their free days and withhold the money they had earned. Such rules could impoverish a whole family in one season. Children were left to starve while the owner grew richer every year. He would intimidate anyone who asked a question, and he would humiliate the youngest workers in front of the rest. The town finally asked him to divest his shares in the mill. Clean hands, the report said, would enrich the whole village. Nothing changed for another year.","zh":"一份报告说，那家老厂剥夺了工人的休息和应得的工钱。老板们扣掉他们的休假日，还把他们挣下的钱压着不发。这样的规矩一个季度就能让一家人穷下来。孩子挨着饿，厂主却一年比一年富。谁要是提个问题，他就吓唬谁，还爱当着别人的面羞辱最年轻的工人。镇上最后要求他把厂里的股份让出去。报告里说，手干净了，整个村子都能富起来。可又过了一年，什么也没变。"},"devise":{"tw":[["prepare",0],["lay",3],["gift",2],["implement",6],["organize",0],["mount",3],["initiate",2],["propose",6],["invent",0]],"en":"To help the children read, a young teacher had to devise a new game for her class. She would prepare a set of cards and lay them out on the floor. It took a week to organize the rules and to mount the pictures on thick board. She liked to propose a small prize for the winning team. The children began to invent their own versions within days. The school agreed to initiate the game in one room first and then to implement it in every class. One parent brought a gift of new cards for the shelf. It was the best change of the whole year.","zh":"为了帮孩子们学会认字，一位年轻女教师得给班上设计一个新游戏。她先做出一套卡片，把它们摊在地上。光是理清规则、把图片贴到厚纸板上，就花了一个星期。她喜欢给赢的那组设一个小奖品。没过几天，孩子们就自己编出了新的玩法。学校同意把这个游戏推广到每个班。有位家长还送来一盒新卡片，放到架子上。那是那一整年里最好的变化。"},"digest":{"tw":[["bear",0],["accept",3],["change",2],["publish",6],["stand",0],["pay",3],["process",2],["journal",6],["support",0]],"en":"Every morning my father would read a short digest of the news with his tea. He could not bear a long report, so he chose a small journal that came to the door. The paper would publish a new list of facts each day. He had to pay for it himself, and he would stand at the counter to chat about the headlines. He liked to accept the facts slowly and let them change his view. A good editor can process a hundred pages into one. His wife said it was the cheapest support he could give.","zh":"每天早上，父亲都会就着茶读一小篇新闻摘要。长的报道他读不下去，所以订了一份送到门口的小刊物。那报纸每天都会登出一份新的事实清单。钱得他自己出，他还爱站在柜台边跟人聊两句头条。他习惯慢慢接受这些消息，再让它们改变自己的看法。好的编辑能把一百页浓缩成一页。他妻子说，这是他花得最值的支持。"},"disperse":{"tw":[["dust",0],["break",3],["separate",2],["riot",6],["spread",0],["carry",3],["discharge",2],["tear",6],["broadcast",0]],"en":"The gates opened at noon, and the guards had to break the long queues into short lines. A slow discharge of visitors lasted until dark, and the dust rose from the dry ground as thousands of feet moved at once. After the last song the crowd began to disperse into the side streets. Some people would separate from their friends and carry a flag home. The news would broadcast a short report about the long wait at the gate. A quarrel near the stage almost turned into a small riot before the guards stepped in. The noise could tear at the ears of anyone close to the speakers. By midnight the square was spread with paper and empty cups.","zh":"中午开门时，保安只好把长队截成一段一段。人流一直散到天黑，几千只脚同时走动，把干地踩起一层灰。最后一首歌唱完，人群开始往两边的小街里散去。有人和同伴走散了，手里还举着旗子回家。新闻里播了一条短短的消息，说的是门口排的长队。舞台边上差点因为口角闹成一场小骚乱，幸好看场的人赶紧插了进来。离音箱近的人，耳朵会被震得生疼。到午夜，广场上摊了一地的纸和空杯子。"},"dock":{"tw":[["tail",2],["moor",3],["cut",2],["barge",6],["pier",0],["marina",3],["enter",2],["ship",6],["wharf",0]],"en":"At dawn the fishing boats would enter the harbour and move slowly toward the dock. Each captain had to moor his boat beside the pier and wait for a free place at the wharf. A small barge would cut through the water and bring boxes of ice. The marina on the far side was full of white boats with long flags at the tail. The dock looked quiet to visitors, but the work never stopped. A young worker would carry a rope from the ship to the post and tie it with fast hands. By seven the market was open and the fish were sold.","zh":"天刚亮，渔船陆续进港，慢慢驶向码头。每位船长得把船拴在栈桥边，等卸货的泊位空出来。一条小船划开水面，把一箱箱冰送过来。对面的游艇湾里停满白船，船尾都挂着长长的旗。在外人看来码头很安静，其实活儿一刻没停。一个年轻工人把缆绳从船上拖到木桩上，几下就系好了。到七点，市场开了张，鱼也都卖了出去。"},"dot":{"tw":[["dust",0],["spray",3],["cover",2],["blue",6],["dose",0],["sprinkle",3],["mark",2],["zip",6],["scatter",0]],"en":"On a paper map my father would mark every well with a small dot. He would cover the streams in blue and sprinkle a thin line of dust to show the dry land. A single spray of ink could scatter across the page if his hand slipped. He liked to zip the maps into clear cases for the wet season, and every report began with a small dose of colour. In the hall of the town office a large map hung on the wall. Children would stand in front of it and ask about the dots. Each one, he told them, was a place where people once found water.","zh":"在纸质地图上，父亲用一个小圆点标出每一口水井。他把河流涂成蓝色，再撒一条细细的粉线，标出干旱的地段。要是手一抖，一小片墨点就会散到整页纸上。他喜欢把地图装进透明袋子里，好在雨季用；每份报告都从一点颜色开始。镇公所的大厅墙上挂着一张大图。孩子们会站在前面，问那些点是什么意思。他告诉他们，每一个都是曾经有人找到水的地方。"},"enlarge":{"tw":[["elaborate",0],["detail",3],["grow",2],["fortify",6],["expand",3],["specify",3],["increase",2],["consolidate",6],["magnify",3]],"en":"When the family shop began to enlarge its stock, we had to detail every new cost in a book. My uncle would elaborate on each plan at dinner until we all knew it by heart. He wanted to grow the business slowly and to consolidate the small debts first. A new wall would fortify the store room against the winter rain. The owner had to specify exactly which shelves would expand with the new goods. A larger window could magnify the whole front of the shop. The increase in visitors was small but real. By spring the place looked twice its size.","zh":"家里的小店一开始扩大货源，我们就得把每一笔新开销记在本子上。吃饭时叔叔会把每个计划细细讲一遍，讲得我们都能背下来。他想把生意慢慢做大，先把小笔欠账并到一起还清。新砌一堵墙，好让仓库扛得住冬天的雨。店主还得写清楚哪些架子要腾出来放新货。换一面大点的玻璃，能把整个店面都放大。来的人是多了些，不算多，却是真的。到春天，这铺子看着大了一倍。"},"exempt":{"tw":[["excuse",0],["forgive",3],["absolve",2],["enforce",1],["provision",6],["free",0],["spare",3],["apply",6],["relieve",0]],"en":"Because of a long illness, one student asked to be exempt from the final test. The school would excuse her from the written part and spare her the group work. Her teacher chose to forgive the late papers and to absolve her of the fine. The office had to apply the same rule to two other cases. A special provision allowed a free retake in the autumn. The head had to enforce it fairly, so that nobody would feel left out. The nurse would relieve her mind with a few kind words. In the end she sat the test in the autumn instead.","zh":"因为病了很长一段时间，有个学生申请免考期末。学校准她不做笔试，也不用参加小组作业。老师愿意不计较迟交的作业，还免掉了她的罚款。办公室得把同一条规矩用到另外两个情况上。有一项特别规定允许她在秋天免费补考。校长得公平地执行，好让谁都不觉得被落下。校医用几句温和的话让她放松下来。最后她在秋天补考了。"},"fascinate":{"tw":[["catch",0],["hold",3],["interest",2],["annoy",6],["charm",0],["work",3],["attract",2],["exasperate",6],["capture",0]],"en":"A room of old clocks can fascinate even a child who hates lessons. The small wheels would catch the eye and hold it for minutes at a time. Their charm could attract a whole crowd to one glass case. A slow tick would annoy nobody, yet it never stopped. My uncle liked to work there and explain how each spring was made. The story of one clock could exasperate the visitors who wanted exact dates. A single photograph would capture the room forever. For me the interest lasted all afternoon.","zh":"一间摆满旧钟的屋子，连最讨厌上课的孩子也会被它迷住。那些小齿轮能抓住人的目光，一看就是好几分钟。它们的魅力能把一群人聚到一个玻璃柜前。慢慢走的嘀嗒声不惹谁烦，却一刻不停。我叔叔喜欢在那儿干活，一边讲每个发条是怎么做出来的。只讲一只钟的来历，会把那些想知道确切年代的人急坏。一张照片就能把这个房间永远留住。对我来说，这份兴趣持续了整个下午。"},"fling":{"tw":[["offer",0],["waste",3],["move",2],["banter",6],["pass",0],["dump",3],["throw",2],["frolic",6],["crack",0]],"en":"On the beach my brother would fling a small stone into the grey water. He liked to throw one after another and never waste a turn. Whenever I made a joke, he would offer a quick answer and we would fall into easy banter. A wave of wind could move the sand under our feet. Two dogs began to frolic near the rocks, and one would dump a wet stick at our feet. A sharp crack of thunder made us pick up our bags and pass the gate fast. The storm came before we reached the car.","zh":"在海滩上，弟弟把一块小石头甩进灰色的海水里。他一块接一块地扔，从不肯浪费一次机会。每次我说个笑话，他都能马上接上一句，我们就这么你一句我一句地聊起来。一阵风把脚下的沙挪动了。两条狗在礁石边撒起欢来，其中一条还把一根湿木棍丢在我们脚边。一声响雷炸开，我们赶紧拎起包往门口跑。还没走到车边，雨就下来了。"},"flock":{"tw":[["deal",0],["flight",3],["meet",2],["congregate",6],["lot",0],["flood",3],["travel",2],["herd",6],["mess",0]],"en":"Every autumn a large flock of birds would travel south over our valley. They would congregate on the flat field before the long flight. A lot of them would meet at the same pond each year, as if by an old agreement. When they took off at once, they looked like a flood of dark wings against the sky. A herd of cows in the next field would stop and watch them go. The whole visit left a mess of feathers and seed on the grass. It was a great deal of noise for three short days.","zh":"每年秋天，一大群鸟都会从我们山谷上空往南飞。长途起飞前，它们先聚在平坦的田里。每年都有很多鸟在同一口池塘边会合，像是早有约定。它们一齐起飞时，天上就像涌过一片黑色的翅膀。旁边地里的牛群会停下来看着它们走。这一趟待完，草地上落了一层羽毛和种子。短短三天，闹出的声响可真不小。"},"forge":{"tw":[["form",0],["chip",3],["beat",2],["consolidate",6],["shape",0],["hill",3],["travel",2],["revive",6],["work",0]],"en":"At the forge near the hill, the blacksmith would beat a bar of hot iron into shape. Small pieces of metal would chip off the surface and fall on the stones. He had to form the curve with slow taps and then let the iron cool. His work would travel to three towns where farmers needed tools. A young helper began to beat the metal too fast and nearly spoiled the blade. Old songs helped revive the mood in the dark shed. All day the two of them would consolidate their small stock of iron. It was hard work, but the ring of the hammer was a kind of music.","zh":"在山边那间铁匠铺里，铁匠把一根烧红的铁条敲出形状。小小的铁屑从表面崩下来，落在石头上。他得用轻轻的锤击一点点把弧度敲出来，再让铁慢慢冷。他打的工具会送到三个镇上，那里的农人正等着用。新来的帮工锤得太急，差点把刀口毁了。几首老歌让昏暗的棚子里又有了点精神。一整天，两人把手里那点铁料整理归拢。活儿很累，可锤子的响声像是一种音乐。"},"fuse":{"tw":[["combine",0],["absorb",3],["melt",2],["defuse",1],["tube",6],["mix",0],["gauge",3],["coil",6],["blend",0]],"en":"In the school lab a thin fuse blew and the lights went out. The teacher had to combine two wires and to absorb the shock of the sudden stop. He would melt a little metal and pour it into a glass tube. Then he had to mix a powder and blend it with water until it turned grey. A small gauge on the wall began to drop toward zero. He used a coil of wire to defuse the danger and make the room safe again. The class learned more in that hour than in a month.","zh":"学校实验室里一根细保险丝烧断了，灯全灭了。老师得把两根线接上，还得稳住这一下的冲击。他把一点金属熔化，倒进一根玻璃管里。接着把一种粉末和水掺到一起，搅成灰色。墙上一只小仪表开始往零掉。他用一圈导线把危险卸掉，让屋子里重新安全下来。那一节课学到的东西，比一个月还多。"},"gauge":{"tw":[["guess",0],["reckon",3],["calculate",2],["curve",6],["judge",0],["assess",3],["distance",2],["grid",6],["approximate",0]],"en":"Before the bridge was built, engineers had to gauge the depth of the river. They would calculate the curve of the bank and the distance between the two sides. A long grid of ropes helped them assess the shape of the ground. No one could guess how much stone the work would need. They had to reckon with the spring flood and add a wide base. Their first numbers were only approximate. A judge would later decide who had to pay for the delay. In the end the bridge stood for forty years.","zh":"修桥之前，工程师得先测出这条河有多深。他们要算出河岸的弧度，还有两岸之间的距离。一张用绳子拉成的方格网帮他们判断地面的形状。谁也猜不准这活儿要用多少石料。他们还得把春汛算进去，把桥基加宽。头一组数字只是大概的。后来有位法官来裁定，延误的钱该谁出。到最后，这座桥立了四十年。"},"graze":{"tw":[["range",0],["grass",3],["feed",2],["forage",6],["crop",0],["shave",3],["brush",2],["herd",6],["pasture",0]],"en":"On the open range above the valley, a herd of sheep would graze from dawn to dusk. They would feed on the short grass and move slowly toward the pasture. In dry months they had to forage along the fence for anything green. A young herder would brush the dust from their wool and shave the heaviest parts. Their crop of wool was small that year, and the family felt it at the market. At night the animals would return to the same corner of the field. In winter the snow would cover the range, and the work moved indoors.","zh":"在山谷上方那片开阔的牧野上，一群羊从早吃到晚。它们啃着短短的草，慢慢往牧场那边挪。旱季里，它们只能沿着围栏找一点绿的东西充饥。年轻的牧人会拂掉羊毛上的土，剪掉最厚的那部分。那一年羊毛的收成不好，一家人在集市上就感到了。夜里羊群总会回到地里同一个角落。到了冬天，雪盖住牧野，活儿就挪到屋里做了。"},"grind":{"tw":[["dig",0],["chew",3],["dance",2],["chop",6],["labour",0],["pulp",3],["press",2],["bump",6],["mill",3]],"en":"At the old mill my aunt would grind corn for the whole village. She had to dig the grain out of the sack and chop the wood for the stove first. The heavy stone would press the kernels into a fine pulp. Her labour began before sunrise, and the dust made her chew on a dry throat. A small bump on the floor could spoil the rhythm, so she never danced around the table. Children came to watch the wheel turn. By noon the sacks were full and the mill was quiet.","zh":"在那座老磨坊里，我姑妈给全村人磨玉米。她得先把粮食从袋子里掏出来，再劈好灶上的柴。沉重的磨盘把玉米粒压成细细的糊。她的活儿天不亮就开始，满屋的粉让她只能干咽着。地上稍微有个凸起就会打乱节奏，所以她从不围着桌子转来转去。孩子们来看那轮子怎么转。到中午，袋子都装满了，磨坊也静下来。"},"hug":{"tw":[["embrace",2],["cuddle",3],["touch",2],["smile",6],["squeeze",0],["interlock",3],["clasp",2],["laugh",6],["clinch",3]],"en":"When my sister came home after two years abroad, the whole family met her at the gate. My mother would embrace her first and then give her a long hug. She wanted to cuddle the baby and would squeeze his small hand. The little one reached out to touch her face and held on. Their hands seemed to interlock like two old rings. Nobody said a word, and a warm smile passed between them. My father would clasp his son's shoulder and laugh at the same old joke. For a second the two brothers would clinch before they walked inside.","zh":"姐姐在国外待了两年回来，一家人都到门口去接。母亲先上去抱住她，抱了很久。她想抱抱孩子，把那小手捏了又捏。小家伙伸手去摸她的脸，不肯放开。两个人的手像两枚旧戒指一样扣在一起。谁也没说话，一个暖暖的笑在她们之间传过。父亲搂了搂儿子的肩，为那句老笑话又笑了一回。兄弟俩在门口先抱了一下，才走进屋。"},"incline":{"tw":[["run",0],["climb",3],["feel",2],["slope",6],["side",0],["fall",3],["listen",2],["gauge",6],["tend",0]],"en":"On the long climb home the path began to incline toward the right side of the hill. We could feel the change in our legs before we saw the slope ahead. My father would listen to the wind and gauge how far we still had to run before dark. The safest way was to tend toward the grass and keep away from the edge. One loose stone could make a walker fall in a second. A cold mist came down, and the whole hill turned grey. Halfway up we sat and drank the last of our water.","zh":"回家那段长坡上，小路开始朝山右侧斜过去。还没看见前面的斜坡，腿就先觉出不对了。父亲会听风的声音，估摸天黑前我们还得走多远。最稳妥的办法是靠草的那一侧走，离崖边远些。一块松动的石头就能让人一秒钟摔下去。冷雾压下来，整座山都成了灰色。爬到半路，我们坐下，把最后一点水喝完了。"},"differentiate":{"tw":[["difference",4],["separate",0],["sex",3],["identify",2],["integrate",1],["distinguish",0],["contrast",3]],"en":"In our birdwatching class the teacher showed us how to differentiate two kinds of sparrow. At first I could not identify the difference between them, because they looked so much alike. She taught us to separate the notes of their songs and to distinguish one call from another. By contrast, the male and the female sang in quite different ways. The sex of a young bird is often the hardest thing to name. Later we tried to integrate all the small marks into one clear picture. By spring I could tell them apart at a distance.","zh":"在观鸟课上，老师教我们怎么区分两种麻雀。起初我认不出它们之间的差别，因为它们长得太像了。她教我们拆开它们鸣叫的音符，把一种叫声和另一种分辨开来。相比之下，雄鸟和雌鸟的唱法大不相同。幼鸟的性别往往是最难叫准的。后来我们试着把那些小特征整合成一幅清晰的图。到春天，我远远地就能把它们分清了。"},"divine":{"tw":[["divinity",4],["lord",0],["god",2],["spirit",6],["ecclesiastic",0],["search",2],["supernatural",6]],"en":"The old chapel on the hill was once a centre of divinity, and its walls still spoke of a divine past. A faded painting above the door showed a lord with a calm face. Villagers said a god had watched over them during the long winters. The spirit of that quiet room could still be felt by every visitor. An ecclesiastic book lay open in a glass case near the back. We began to search the records for the name of the painter, but found none. Some people call such a feeling supernatural, though I simply called it peace.","zh":"山上的那座老礼拜堂，曾是一处研究神学的中心，它的墙壁至今仍在诉说着一段神圣的往事。门上方一幅褪色的画里，画着一位面容平静的主。村民们说，在漫长的冬天里，有位神一直看顾着他们。每位走进来的人，都还能感到那间静室里的气息。后边一个玻璃柜里摊着一本教会的书。我们开始翻查记录，想找出画家的名字，却一无所获。有人把这种感觉称作超自然，而我只当它是一份宁静。"},"furnish":{"tw":[["furniture",4],["provide",0],["bed",3],["configure",6],["supply",2],["glass",3],["render",0]],"en":"When my cousin moved into her first small flat, she had to furnish it on a tight budget. A neighbour offered to provide an old table and a wooden bed. She would supply the kitchen herself with cheap glass cups and a few pans. It took a whole day to configure the tiny room so that everything could fit. The heavy furniture had to be carried up three floors, which would render her arms weak. By evening the flat looked warm and lived in. She said a home is built slowly, one piece at a time.","zh":"表姐搬进她第一间小公寓时，手头很紧，也得把家具置办起来。一位邻居愿意提供一张旧桌子和一张木床。她自己买来便宜的玻璃杯和几口锅凑齐厨房。要把这小房间布置得样样放得下，花了一整天。沉重的家具得搬上三层楼，把她的胳膊都累软了。到傍晚，公寓看着暖和，也有了住人的味道。她说，一个家是一点一点慢慢搭起来的。"},"gut":{"tw":[["gutter",4],["bowel",0],["empty",2],["stomach",6],["intestine",0],["channel",2],["bite",6]],"en":"After two weeks of a heavy stomach, my uncle went to the clinic for a check. The doctor said a problem in the gut could make a person feel empty and weak all day. She asked about his bowel and whether his intestine had ever been treated before. A small camera was sent down a thin channel to look for the cause, and she told him not to bite his lip. Rain ran down the gutter outside as we waited for the result. The news was good, and a change of food would help. He laughed and said he would miss his old meals.","zh":"胃里难受了两周之后，叔叔去了诊所检查。医生说，肠道出了毛病，会让人整天觉得空落落、没力气。她问了问他的排便情况，以及他的肠子以前有没有治过。一根细管把一台小相机送进去查找原因，她还叫他别咬嘴唇。我们等结果的时候，雨水顺着外面的排水沟流下去。结果是好的，换换饮食就有帮助。他笑着说，他会想念从前那些饭菜。"},"deteriorate":{"tw":[["drop",0],["tire",3],["decay",2],["recuperate",1],["exacerbate",6],["degenerate",0],["waste",3],["aggravate",6]],"en":"The old road began to deteriorate as we drove further from town. A sharp drop in the surface made the wheels shake and our bags slide. My father would tire quickly, so we stopped to rest every hour. Rust and rain had made the guard rail decay and degenerate into thin metal. 'Do not aggravate the engine,' he said, 'and do not waste good fuel by pushing it too hard.' Hurrying would only exacerbate the small problem, so we kept a slow speed. After three days of rest, the car seemed to recuperate, and we reached home.","zh":"我们离城越走越远，那条旧路也开始变坏。路面一处突然塌下去，震得轮子直抖，包也滑来滑去。父亲很快就累，我们每小时就停下来歇一歇。铁锈和雨水让护栏慢慢锈蚀、退化成薄薄一层铁。他说：'别硬拖着发动机，也别猛踩油门白白费油。'急着赶路只会让这个小毛病更糟，所以我们一直开得很慢。歇了三天，车子像是缓了过来，我们才到了家。"},"devil":{"tw":[["bother",0],["harass",3],["cook",2],["curse",6],["irritate",0],["fret",3],["magic",6],["demon",0]],"en":"Our old oven had become a real little devil in the kitchen. It would bother my mother every time she tried to cook. The heat would either burn the food or stay cold, which began to irritate her badly. She would curse the machine and fret over the wasted meal. 'There is no magic in this thing,' she said, 'only rust and bad wires.' Still, she refused to let a small demon like that harass her all winter. One day a repairman came with new parts, and the oven obeyed at last.","zh":"我们那台旧烤箱，成了厨房里真正的小魔鬼。每次妈妈想做饭，它都要捣乱。火候不是把菜烤糊，就是一直不热，这把她气得够呛。她会骂这机器，还为糟蹋掉的饭菜发愁。她说：'这玩意儿里没有什么魔法，只有锈和坏电线。'可她就是不肯让这么个小鬼头缠着她一整个冬天。有一天，修理工带着新零件来了，烤箱终于听话了。"},"dip":{"tw":[["drop",0],["dabble",3],["lower",2],["tumble",6],["fall",0],["angle",2],["slide",6],["duck",0]],"en":"On a wet Sunday I had to dip my brush into the paint again and again. A sharp drop of rain would fall on the wet wood and make me start over. I had to lower the brush at a careful angle so the line stayed straight. Once a small can began to slide and nearly tumbled off the stand. A duck walked past the gate while I dabbled the last corner with colour. When the storm came, I had to pick up my tools and run inside. By evening the fence looked even and bright.","zh":"一个下雨的星期天，我一遍又一遍地把刷子蘸进油漆里。一滴急雨会落在湿木头上，逼我重新来。我得把刷子按一个稳当的角度放低，线条才直。有一次小漆罐开始滑动，差点从架子上摔下来。一只鸭子从门口走过，那时我正胡乱涂着最后一个角。暴风雨一来，我只好收拾工具跑进屋。到傍晚，围栏看着又匀又亮。"},"discard":{"tw":[["dispose",0],["waste",3],["object",2],["scrape",6],["toss",0],["dump",3],["rub",6],["fling",0]],"en":"On a clear morning we began to clean the old garage and discard what we no longer needed. My father would toss a broken chair aside and dump the rusty cans in a pile. 'Do not waste good tools,' he said, 'or simply fling them away.' I had to scrape the mud off one metal object before I could see its shape. I would rub the dust from a lamp that still worked. We had to dispose of the rest in a safe place. By noon the floor was empty and bright.","zh":"一个晴朗的早上，我们开始清理旧车库，把不再需要的东西丢掉。父亲把一把坏椅子扔到一边，把锈罐头倒成一堆。他说：'别把好工具浪费掉，也别随手就甩了。'我得先把一个金属物件上的泥刮掉，才看得出它的形状。我又把一盏还能亮的灯上的灰擦掉。剩下的得送到安全的地方处理掉。到中午，地面空了，也亮堂了。"},"distract":{"tw":[["trouble",0],["worry",3],["confuse",2],["embarrass",6],["disorder",0],["disturb",2],["intimidate",6],["deflect",0]],"en":"In the middle of the test, a loud noise from the hall began to distract me. My trouble was that I could not stop looking at the door. Worry over my low score began to confuse my thoughts. I did not want to embarrass myself by standing up too early. The disorder on my desk, with papers everywhere, did not help at all. I tried to deflect every sound and disturb no one around me. In the end I told myself the teacher would not try to intimidate us. Slowly my mind cleared and I finished the page.","zh":"考试进行到一半，走廊里一阵响声开始让我分心。我的麻烦是，我总忍不住去看那扇门。担心分数太低，又搅乱了我的思路。我不想太早站起来，让自己难堪。桌子上乱七八糟，纸到处都是，一点忙都帮不上。我努力把每一种声音都挡开，也不去打扰周围的人。最后我告诉自己，老师不会成心吓唬我们。慢慢地，脑子清楚了，我把那张卷子做完了。"},"dull":{"tw":[["slow",0],["cloud",3],["change",2],["bright",1],["bit",6],["damp",0],["downright",6],["dim",0]],"en":"The long bus ride through the flat county felt dull after the first hour. A slow rain began to cloud the windows and dim the light inside. There was not a bit of colour in the fields, only grey sky and damp grass. I hoped the trip would change and bring something bright at the next stop. The driver was a downright quiet man who said almost nothing. After a while I closed my eyes, and the dull noise of the engine rocked me to sleep. When I woke, the sun was out.","zh":"穿过平坦乡村的长途汽车，坐过一个小时就让人觉得乏味。细雨开始糊住车窗，把车里的光也弄暗了。田野里没有一点颜色，只有灰天和湿草。我盼着这趟旅程能变一变，到下一站能见到点亮色。司机是个十足沉默的人，几乎什么都不说。过了一会儿我闭上眼，单调的引擎声把我摇睡着了。等我醒来，太阳已经出来了。"},"erupt":{"tw":[["break",0],["catch",3],["trouble",2],["escalate",6],["burst",0],["explode",2],["inflame",6],["flare",0]],"en":"In the small office a quarrel could erupt over the smallest, silliest thing. That morning a broken order made two clerks catch each other's words and start to shout at once. The trouble had begun days before, when a bill was filed in the wrong box. Tempers would flare and the whole room seemed ready to burst. I feared that the fight might escalate into something far worse. One of them tried to inflame the other by repeating an old mistake. In the end the manager stepped in just before the argument could explode.","zh":"在这间小办公室里，最不起眼的小事都可能引爆一场争吵。那天早上，一张订单出了错，两个文员就你一句我一句地嚷了起来。麻烦其实几天前就开始了，一张账单被放错了格子。火气一上来，整间屋子眼看着就要炸开。我担心这场架会越闹越大。其中一人翻出旧账，想给对方火上浇油。最后，经理在争吵彻底爆发之前赶了进来。"},"escort":{"tw":[["date",0],["usher",3],["accompany",2],["patrol",6],["see",0],["convoy",3],["companion",2],["fleet",6]],"en":"On the school trip two teachers had to escort forty children through the old museum. One would usher the line past each door and count them again and again. A guard had to patrol the yard and keep the gate shut. My classmate asked me to accompany her to the far hall, where the old maps were kept. She wrote down the date of our next visit and said I was her best companion on any trip. A small convoy of buses waited outside, and a fleet of taxis stood behind them. I promised to see every child back to the bus before dark. On the way home we sang, and no one was lost or late.","zh":"学校组织出游时，两位老师得护送四十个孩子穿过那座老博物馆。一位领着队伍走过每道门，一遍又一遍地点人数。一名保安得在院子里巡逻，看住大门。同学叫我陪她去摆放旧地图的远处展厅。她记下了我们下次来的日期，还说任何一趟出游我都是她最好的伙伴。外面停着一小队公交车，后面还排着一列出租车。我答应天黑前把每个孩子都送上大巴。回家的路上我们一路唱歌，谁也没走丢，也没人迟到。"},"fake":{"tw":[["cook",0],["juggle",3],["cheat",2],["bogus",6],["manipulate",0],["feign",2],["phony",6]],"en":"My cousin once tried to buy a watch from a man at a beach market. The seller would juggle three boxes in his hands and talk about the fine price. He seemed to cook up a story about a famous maker, but every word was bogus. My cousin did not want to be cheated, so he asked to see the small print. The man began to feign surprise, then tried to manipulate the price with a sad face. It was clear that the shiny watch was phony and that the whole deal was a fake. We walked away before he could change his mind. The lesson was simple: a smooth tongue is not a true one.","zh":"我表弟曾在海滩集市上向一个男人买表。那人一边在手里抛接三个盒子，一边夸价钱公道。他像是编了个关于名匠的故事，可每个字都是假的。我表弟不想被骗，就要求看那些小字。那人先假装吃惊，又装出一副可怜相想操控价格。很明显，那块亮闪闪的表是赝品，整桩买卖都是骗局。我们没等他再改口就走开了。道理很简单：嘴甜不等于真心。"},"flap":{"tw":[["beat",2],["tongue",3],["move",2],["cuff",6],["roll",0],["lap",3],["scar",6],["wave",2]],"en":"On a windy afternoon I took my dog down to the cold shore. A red flag began to flap above the small hut, and the wind would beat against my coat. My dog's ears could not stop their little wave, and his long tongue hung out as he ran. A grey wave would roll in and the water would lap the wet stones near our feet. I rolled up the cuff of my sleeve and let him drink. On his back leg I could see an old scar from a bad winter. Then the wind grew stronger, and we had to move toward the car. The drive home was quiet, and he slept the whole way.","zh":"一个有风的下午，我带着狗去了冰凉的海边。小木屋上方的红旗开始拍打，风一下下打在我的外套上。狗的耳朵不住地轻轻摆动，一条长舌头耷拉着，跟着他跑。一道灰浪卷上来，水舔着我们脚边湿漉漉的石子。我卷起袖口，让他喝水。他后腿上有一道旧疤，是某个坏冬天留下的。后来风更大了，我们只好往车那边挪。回家的路很安静，他一路上睡到了家。"},"flick":{"tw":[["film",0],["feature",3],["move",2],["caper",6],["picture",0],["documentary",3],["push",2],["flip",0]],"en":"My neighbour runs a small film club in an old hall on Fridays. Last week he chose a short flick from an unknown maker, then a longer feature about a village band. The picture was black and white, so we had to push the old machine to keep the light steady. It was not a serious documentary but a light caper with two thieves and a stolen car. Nobody wanted to move during the funny parts. In the second half the reel began to flip and the sound cut out. He fixed it, and we clapped. It was the cheapest night out I have had all year.","zh":"我邻居每周五在一座旧礼堂里办一个小电影俱乐部。上周他先放了一部无名作者拍的短片，接着是一部长片，讲一支乡村乐队。片子是黑白的，我们得推着那台老机器才让光稳住。它不是严肃的纪录片，而是一出轻松闹剧，讲两个小偷和一辆被偷的车。好笑的地方谁也不想动。下半场胶片开始翻，声音也断了。他修好了，我们就鼓起掌。这是我这一年里最便宜的一次消遣。"},"flourish":{"tw":[["wave",2],["revive",3],["grow",2],["evolve",6],["boom",0],["move",2],["adapt",6],["expand",0]],"en":"Ten years ago the market on our street began to flourish again. A young couple would wave to every neighbour and open a tiny bread stall at dawn. Slowly their trade began to grow, and they had to move to a bigger corner to fit the crowd. To adapt to new tastes, they let the old recipes evolve into lighter ones. When the town held its summer fair, a short boom helped them sell everything they had. They even managed to expand the shop and revive a small garden behind it. Today the smell of fresh bread marks the street. Hard work, not luck, made the little stall flourish.","zh":"十年前，我们这条街上的集市又兴旺起来。一对年轻夫妻会跟每个邻居挥手，天一亮就支起一个很小的面包摊。生意慢慢长大，他们不得不换到更大的角落才容得下客人。为了适应新口味，他们让老配方一点点变得清淡。镇上办夏季庙会时，一阵短暂的景气让他们把货全卖光了。他们甚至把小店扩大，还让屋后的小园子重新活了起来。如今，烤面包的香味就是这条街的记号。是肯吃苦，而不是运气，让这个小摊兴旺起来。"},"flush":{"tw":[["charge",0],["grade",3],["run",2],["wipe",6],["flower",0],["water",2],["squeeze",6],["kick",0]],"en":"My sister wakes early, has a short run, and comes home with her cheeks in a hot flush. She kicks off her shoes at the door, then wipes her face with a cold cloth. The flowers she planted last spring are now in full bloom, a bright flush of colour. She will water them one by one and squeeze a lemon for her tea. The seed came from a cheap bag, sold as a low grade, yet it did well. Her small dog likes to charge across the beds, so she calls him back. By eight she is calm, and the whole yard glows. It is her favourite hour of the day.","zh":"我姐姐起得早，跑一小段，回家时两颊热得通红。她在门口踢掉鞋，然后用凉布擦脸。她去年春天种的花现在开得正盛，一片鲜亮的颜色。她会一棵棵浇水，再挤一颗柠檬泡茶。种子是从一个便宜袋子里来的，标的是低等品，可长势很好。她的小狗爱冲过花畦，她就把它喊回来。到八点她就静下来，整个院子都发起光来。这是她一天里最爱的时刻。"},"fog":{"tw":[["cloud",0],["overshadow",3],["hide",2],["rain",6],["mist",3],["aerosol",2],["snow",6],["obscure",0]],"en":"A thick fog crept over the harbour before the first boat left. Low cloud and cold mist would hide the far shore, so the captain could not see the lights. A thin rain began, and a fine aerosol of salt water hung in the air. The fog seemed to obscure every sign and to overshadow the whole pier. Snow had fallen the night before and still lay on the roofs. We could only wait and listen to the horns. By ten the sun broke through and the grey veil began to lift. The boats moved out, slow and careful, into the open water.","zh":"头一条船开出去之前，一层浓雾爬上了港口。低云和冷雾遮住了远处的岸，船长看不见灯。细雨下起来，细细的带盐的水汽悬在空气里。浓雾仿佛把每块牌子都抹掉了，也压住了整个码头。前一晚下过雪，屋顶上还留着。我们只能等着，听那些汽笛。到十点，太阳透了出来，灰蒙蒙的幕布开始拉开。船一条条慢慢小心地驶向开阔的水面。"},"forbid":{"tw":[["prevent",0],["bar",3],["permit",1],["violate",6],["prohibit",0],["stop",3],["contravene",6],["veto",0]],"en":"The manager of our building had to forbid bikes in the front hall after a bad week. A new rule would prohibit any wheel inside, and a wooden bar now blocks the door. The aim was to prevent small accidents near the stairs. Some workers chose to violate the rule anyway and left their bikes by the wall. The manager could not permit that, so he put up a clear sign. Anyone who wished to contravene it would face a short talk. The owner even had the power to veto the whole plan, but he agreed with it. Cars must stop at the gate, and the hall stays clean.","zh":"熬过一个糟糕的星期后，我们楼的管理员只好禁止在前厅放自行车。新规定不许任何轮子进门，一根木条现在挡住门口。这么做是为了防止楼梯边出小事故。有些员工还是偏要违反，把车靠在墙边。管理员不能允许这样，就贴了一张醒目的告示。谁想违抗，就得被叫去谈一谈。房主甚至有权否决整个方案，但他也表示赞同。车必须停在大门口，前厅也就一直干干净净。"},"fork":{"tw":[["branch",2],["twig",3],["lift",2],["brook",6],["separate",0],["shape",2],["bend",6],["ramification",0]],"en":"On Sunday we followed a narrow path that ran beside a small brook. The trail had a fork, so we had to choose which way to go. A heavy branch lay across the water, with one thin twig caught in the mud. My father would lift the branch and bend down to look at the broken end. He said the shape of a tree shows where each limb will separate and grow. Every little ramification, he told us, carries water to the leaves. We sat on a stone and watched the stream. Then we took the left path and walked home slowly.","zh":"星期天，我们沿着一条挨着小溪的窄路走。小路分了岔，我们得选走哪边。一根粗树枝横在水面上，一小截细枝卡在泥里。父亲把树枝抬起来，弯下腰看那个断口。他说，一棵树的形状能看出每个枝条从哪里分开、又往哪里长。他告诉我们，每一条细小的分枝都在把水送到叶子上。我们坐在一块石头上看溪水。后来我们走了左边那条路，慢慢走回家。"},"fort":{"tw":[["fortify",4],["trench",3],["meet",2],["near",6],["fortress",0],["station",2],["confederate",6],["garrison",0]],"en":"Last spring our class climbed to an old fort on the hill above the town. The guide said the people there would fortify the walls with stone and mud. A deep trench still ran along the outer edge, and a low garrison once kept watch from the stones. From that fortress you could see every road for miles. The soldiers would meet at a small station near the gate before each long night. When enemies came close, several villages would confederate to defend the pass. The hill was quiet now, and only sheep walked there. I stood on the grass and tried to picture the old walls again.","zh":"去年春天，我们班爬到镇子上方山岗上的一座旧堡垒。向导说，当年那里的人会用石头和泥把墙加固。外墙边还留着一道深壕沟，曾有一小队驻军从石头上守望。站在这座要塞上，方圆好些路都能看见。士兵们会在每次漫长的守夜前，到门口那个小哨站集合。敌人逼近时，几个村子会联合起来守住山口。如今山岗很静，只有羊在上面走。我站在草地上，努力在脑子里重新拼出那些旧墙。"},"gamble":{"tw":[["chance",0],["bet",3],["try",2],["adventure",0],["play",3],["firm",6],["risk",2]],"en":"Two years ago my uncle made a quiet gamble and opened a second shop across town. His small firm had little cash, and the manager warned him about the risk. 'Take a chance,' he told us, 'but do not bet the whole house.' He would play with the numbers for nights, then decide to try the new street. The first month brought few buyers, and the shop felt like a slow adventure with no map. By winter, though, regular customers arrived and the gamble paid off. He never told his brother how close he came to losing it. Now he plans a third shop, more carefully.","zh":"两年前，我叔叔悄悄赌了一把，在城那头开了第二家店。他那家小公司没什么现金，经理还提醒过他风险。他说，'抓住机会吧，但别把整个家底都押上。'他抱着数字琢磨了好几个晚上，最后决定去那条新街试试。头一个月没什么顾客，那店像一场没有地图的慢冒险。可到了冬天，老顾客来了，这一赌也值了。他从没跟他哥哥说，自己差一点就赔光了。如今他又在计划开第三家，这回小心多了。"},"glamour":{"tw":[["witch",0],["spell",3],["beauty",2],["fashion",6],["enchant",0],["charm",2],["allure",6],["bewitch",0]],"en":"My grandmother loves to tell a tale about an old theatre and its glamour. In her story a young witch would put a spell on anyone who sat too long in the front row. Her beauty was famous, and her charm could enchant a whole crowd. People said she had the power to bewitch even the coldest guest. Under the bright lights, her allure was stronger than any fashion of that year. She never left the stage, because the room held a strange magic. My grandmother would lower her voice at the end. Then she would smile and turn off the lamp.","zh":"我奶奶爱讲一个故事，说的是一座老剧院和它的魅力。在她的故事里，有个年轻女巫会给在前排坐太久的人施咒。她的美貌出了名，她的一颦一笑能让满场人着迷。人们说，她连最冷的客人也能迷住。亮灯之下，她的吸引力比那一年任何一种时髦都强。她从不下台，因为那间屋子有种奇特的魔力。讲到最后，奶奶会把声音压低。然后她一笑，把灯关掉。"},"glare":{"tw":[["blaze",0],["beat",3],["stare",2],["glow",6],["glower",0],["shine",2],["flashlight",6],["limelight",0]],"en":"On the night of the school play, the old lamps threw a hard glare across the stage. We could feel the heat beat down as if a small blaze burned above us. A bright flashlight in the back row kept shining straight into our eyes. Every actor had to stare at the floor and hide a nervous smile. One boy began to glower at the light, which only made the crowd laugh. When the main singer stepped into the limelight, her dress caught a soft glow. Someone fixed the lamp, and the room grew calm again. We finished the play without another mistake.","zh":"学校演出那晚，几盏旧灯在舞台上投下一片刺眼的强光。我们能感到热气直压下来，仿佛头顶烧着一小团火。后排一支亮手电一直直射进我们眼里。每个演员都得盯着地板，藏住紧张的笑。一个男孩开始朝那灯怒目而视，反倒把大家逗笑了。当主唱走进聚光灯时，她的裙子映出一层柔光。有人把灯修好，屋里又安静下来。我们没再出错，把戏演完了。"},"gleam":{"tw":[["shine",0],["shimmer",3],["look",2],["twinkle",6],["glow",0],["flash",2],["exude",6],["glitter",0]],"en":"Late at night we walked to the lake and watched the water gleam under a thin moon. The whole surface would shimmer with each small wave, and a single star seemed to twinkle above the hills. A faint glow came from the far shore, where a few windows still shone. When a car passed on the road, its lights would flash across the trees. My sister said the lake seemed to exude a calm that she could not explain. I turned to look at her, and her eyes had the same glitter. We stood there for a long while without speaking. Then the cold wind sent us home.","zh":"深夜我们走到湖边，看水在一弯薄月下泛着微光。每起一道小浪，整个水面就闪闪发亮，一颗星星仿佛在山头上眨眼。远处岸边飘着一点淡光，那里还有几扇窗亮着。有车从路上经过时，车灯就在树间闪一下。我妹妹说，这湖仿佛散发着一种她说不上来的安宁。我转过头看她，她的眼里也有同样的光泽。我们在那儿站了很久，一句话也没说。后来冷风把我们送回了家。"},"glide":{"tw":[["coast",3],["plane",3],["fly",2],["flutter",6],["slide",0],["snake",3],["move",2],["drift",6]],"en":"At dusk the small boat began to glide down the quiet river. We would drift past the reeds while a grey plane crossed the sky above us. A pair of white birds seemed to fly low, then flutter over the water and land. Below the surface a long snake would slide between the stones. My father let the boat coast near the bank, and nobody wanted to move. A leaf would move slowly on the still surface beside us. The whole evening seemed to glide by without a sound. Then the first lamp came on at the far bridge, and we turned home.","zh":"黄昏时，小船开始顺流滑行。我们漂过芦苇丛，头顶有一架灰色的飞机掠过天空。一对白鸟低低地飞着，在掠过水面后轻轻扑动翅膀落下。水下有一条长蛇在石头间滑过去。父亲让船贴着岸边滑行，谁也不愿动一下。一片叶子在我们身旁静静的水面上慢慢打转。整个傍晚仿佛无声地滑了过去。后来远处桥头亮起第一盏灯，我们就掉头回家了。"},"gossip":{"tw":[["visit",0],["cat",3],["report",2],["tabloid",6],["chat",2],["scandal",3],["drudge",6],["comment",0]],"en":"In our small street the gossip always starts at the little shop on the corner. Anyone who comes to visit will hear the latest chat about the new family next door. One neighbour reads a cheap tabloid and brings us a full report each morning. Last month a small scandal about a missing garden gate kept the whole street busy for a week. My aunt, who would drudge in the bakery all day, still found time to comment on it. Even her old cat seemed to listen from the window. Nobody ever learned what really happened to the gate. By winter everyone had found a new story to gossip about.","zh":"在我们这条小街上，闲话总是从街角那家小店开始。谁来串门，都会听到隔壁新搬来那家人的最新闲谈。有个邻居每天早上看一份廉价小报，然后带回一份完整的消息。上个月，一桩关于失踪院门的小丑闻让整条街热闹了一个星期。我姑妈在面包店干了一整天苦活，还是能抽空评论两句。连她那只看家的老猫都像是趴在窗边听着。那扇门到底怎么了，谁也没弄明白。到了冬天，大家又找到了新的谈资。"},"hammer":{"tw":[["pound",0],["maul",3],["beat",2],["stick",6],["forge",0],["blow",2],["metal",6]],"en":"An old smith worked in the low shed at the end of our lane. With a heavy hammer he would pound a hot bar until it grew thin and bright. He had a metal maul too, but he liked the small one more. Each blow sent sparks across the floor, and the noise would beat against the walls. Sometimes he would forge a garden tool or mend a bent wheel. I used to stick my head in the door and watch for hours. Once he caught me and tilted his head with a quiet smile. Then he handed me a warm nail and told me to be careful.","zh":"一位老铁匠在我们巷子尽头那间矮棚里干活。他用一把重锤捶打烧红的铁条，直到它变薄发亮。他也有把铁大槌，但他更喜欢那把小的。每一锤都溅出火星，响声撞在墙上。有时他会打一件园艺工具，或修一只弯了的轮子。我以前总把头探进门里，一看就是好几个钟头。有一次他逮住我，偏过头轻轻一笑。然后他递给我一根温热的钉子，让我小心点。"},"harass":{"tw":[["plague",0],["torment",3],["annoy",2],["intimidate",6],["hassle",0],["haze",3],["confuse",6]],"en":"That summer a group of older boys began to harass a quiet new student at camp. They would plague him with small jokes from morning till night. At first it was only a mild haze of teasing, yet it soon turned cruel. They tried to intimidate him so that he would not speak to the leaders. The noise would annoy everyone in the cabin and confuse the younger children. When the staff learned of the hassle, they called a meeting at once. No one was allowed to torment another camper again. The boy stayed, and by August he had made real friends.","zh":"那年夏天，一伙大孩子开始在夏令营欺负一个安静的新同学。他们从早到晚用些小玩笑折磨他。起初只是轻轻起哄，可很快就变得刻薄。他们想威吓他，让他不敢去找带队的老师说话。那些吵闹让整个木屋的人都心烦，也把小孩子弄糊涂。老师知道这场纠缠后，立刻开了个会。从此谁也不许再欺负别的营员。那男孩留了下来，到八月他交到了真正的朋友。"},"harvest":{"tw":[["crop",0],["cut",3],["gather",2],["corn",6],["reap",0],["remove",2],["maize",6],["glean",0]],"en":"Every September the whole family helps bring in the harvest on the small farm. My uncle will cut the corn first and leave the tall stalks to dry in the sun. Then we gather the maize into wide baskets and carry them to the barn. The main crop this year was heavier than last, so the work took three full days. At noon we sit under the tree and rest our arms. Nobody is allowed to remove anything from the field until the last row is done. In the evening we reap what is left and let the poor glean the fallen seeds. It is hard work, but the full barn is worth it.","zh":"每年九月，全家人都来这个小农场帮忙收庄稼。我叔叔先割下玉米，把高高的秆留在太阳下晒干。然后我们把玉米棒收进大篮子，扛到谷仓去。今年主要的收成比去年重，这活干了整整三天。中午我们坐在树下歇胳膊。在最后一垄收完前，谁也不许从地里拿走东西。傍晚我们把剩下的都收了，让穷人来捡掉在地上的谷粒。活很累，可粮仓装满就值了。"},"haul":{"tw":[["catch",0],["tow",3],["pull",2],["freight",6],["draw",0],["transport",2],["spare",6],["cart",0]],"en":"At four in the morning the small crew began to haul the heavy nets onto the deck. They had to pull with both arms, and the wet rope would draw blood from their hands. A second boat came to tow a broken engine back to the harbour. By six a long freight train passed the docks, loaded with boxes for the city. My father would transport the catch to the market in an old cart. He always kept a spare rope under the seat for a sudden break. The biggest catch that day was a single silver fish. We sold it before the sun was high, and the work felt light.","zh":"凌晨四点，小船上的几个船员开始把沉重的渔网拖上甲板。他们得用两只胳膊使劲拉，湿绳把他们的手都勒出了血。第二条船过来，把一台坏掉的发动机拖回港口。六点时，一列长长的货运列车驶过码头，车上装满发往城里的箱子。父亲会用一辆旧板车把渔获运到市场。他座位底下总留着一根备用绳，以防突然断裂。那天最大的一网只有一条银色的鱼。太阳还没升高我们就把它卖了，活儿也显得轻了。"},"hood":{"tw":[["cap",0],["bully",3],["cover",2],["rear",6],["tough",0],["criminal",2],["green",6],["punk",0]],"en":"On a cold morning a group of tough boys stood at the rear of the school gate. One pulled his hood over his head and another wore a flat cap. A local bully liked to frighten the younger kids with loud words. Their leader, a green boy who wanted to look like a punk, talked of a famous criminal he had read about. The teacher asked them to cover their faces and come inside. She said no one here was a hero for being rough. Slowly the group moved toward the door. By the bell, the yard was quiet again.","zh":"一个清冷的早上，一群硬气的男孩站在校门后头。一个把兜帽拉过头顶，另一个戴着顶平檐帽。本地一个爱欺负人的家伙喜欢用大嗓门吓唬小孩。他们的头儿是个想装成混混的毛头小子，嘴里念叨着从书上看到的一个有名罪犯。老师让他们把脸遮好，进屋去。她说在这儿没人因为粗野就成了英雄。那群人慢慢朝门口挪去。上课铃响时，操场又安静了。"},"idle":{"tw":[["dead",0],["moon",3],["busy",1],["empty",6],["light",0],["bum",3],["pitch",6],["wild",0]],"en":"When the old factory closed, the whole street grew idle and quiet. The big building stood empty, and no light burned in its long windows. A few men would bum around the gate, waiting for work that never came. Under a pale moon the place looked dead, not busy as it once was. The manager said the plant could sit idle for a year, or maybe more. Some kids played in the wild grass that now covered the yard. At midnight it was pitch dark, and the silence felt strange. Everyone hoped the machines would run again one day.","zh":"老厂子一关，整条街就闲了下来，静悄悄的。那栋大楼空着，长长的窗户里再没有一盏灯亮。几个男人在门口晃荡，等着永远不来的活。淡淡的月光下，这地方看着死气沉沉，不再像从前那样忙碌。管理员说，这厂子可能就这么停着，一停就是一年，甚至更久。孩子们在如今长满院子的野草里玩。半夜里一片漆黑，那份安静让人觉得怪。大家都盼着机器哪天再转起来。"},"defect":{"tw":[["flaw",0],["bug",3],["disadvantage",2],["congenital",6],["shortcoming",0],["failure",6],["blemish",0]],"en":"In the factory every worker had to look for a small defect before packing. A tiny flaw in the metal could spoil a whole machine. The boss said each bug must be found and written down. This design had one clear disadvantage and one real shortcoming: it was hard to clean. A single failure in one part could stop the whole line. One buyer worried about a blemish on the painted side. The manager said a weak heart was a congenital fault no test could catch. So they checked every piece twice before it left.","zh":"厂里每个工人在装箱前都得找出细小的瑕疵。金属上一道小小的裂痕就能毁掉整台机器。老板说，每一个缺陷都得找出来、记下来。这个设计有个明显的短处，也有个真正的缺点：不好清理。一个零件出故障，就能让整条线停住。有位买主担心漆面上的一块斑点。经理说，心脏的毛病是先天带来的，什么检测也查不出。所以每件东西出厂前，他们都要查两遍。"},"deficiency":{"tw":[["want",0],["absence",3],["need",2],["anaemia",6],["lack",0],["deficit",3],["hypertension",6]],"en":"The doctor said the tired student had a clear deficiency of iron in his blood. A long lack of good food had slowly weakened him. There was a total absence of fresh vegetables in his daily meals. He did not want to eat much, and his body began to show it. The nurse warned that anaemia could grow worse without care. She said his need for rest was as great as his need for meat. A small deficit in his diet, she added, could also raise his pressure. Long-term hypertension, she said, was the last thing he needed.","zh":"医生说，这个累坏了的学生血里明显缺铁。长期吃不好，把他一点点拖虚了。他每日的饭里，新鲜蔬菜一点都没有。他不想多吃，身体也就显出样子来了。护士警告说，再不好好调养，贫血还会加重。她说，他对休息的需要，和对肉的需要一样大。她又说，饮食上小小的一点亏空，也会让血压升上去。她说，长期的高血压，是他最不需要的东西。"},"disguise":{"tw":[["mask",3],["masquerade",3],["hide",2],["conceal",6],["camouflage",3],["attire",2],["fake",6]],"en":"For the school party every child came dressed in a strange disguise. One wore a paper mask and a long dark coat as his attire. Another chose a bright feather cape to hide his face. My sister used a cheap fake hat and a painted smile. We had to conceal our names until the games were done. A quiet boy in green, in full camouflage, won the first prize. Later the whole class began a happy masquerade in the hall. By eight the masks were off, and everyone looked like themselves.","zh":"学校办晚会，每个孩子都打扮得古里古怪。一个戴着纸面具，外面罩件深色长外衣，就算他的行头。另一个披了件鲜艳的羽毛披风，用来遮脸。我妹妹用了一顶便宜的假帽子，还画了个笑脸。游戏结束前，我们都得把名字藏起来。一个穿绿衣、全身迷彩的安静男孩得了一等奖。后来全班在礼堂里玩起开心的化装舞会。到八点，面具一摘，大家又都像自己了。"},"distress":{"tw":[["hurt",0],["pressure",3],["pain",2],["alarm",6],["wound",3],["trouble",2],["shock",6]],"en":"On the third day of the climb the old guide showed real distress in his face. A deep wound on his leg had begun to hurt with every step. The cold pressure of the wind made the pain even worse. We knew this was trouble, and the whole group felt a sharp shock. He tried not to show his alarm to the young walkers. We sent a call for help and waited by the rocks. A team arrived before dark with warm coats and food. The guide smiled, but he did not walk again that week.","zh":"登山第三天，那位老向导脸上露出了真正的痛苦。他腿上有一道很深的伤口，每走一步都疼。风里那股冷冷的压力，让疼痛更厉害了。我们知道这是麻烦，全队都感到一阵剧痛般的震惊。他尽量不让年轻的同行看出自己的惊慌。我们发出求救，在岩石边等着。天黑前，一支队伍带着厚外套和食物赶到了。向导笑了，可那一周他没再走路。"},"domain":{"tw":[["field",0],["class",2],["function",6],["land",0],["environment",2],["binary",6],["world",0]],"en":"My cousin spends his evenings in a wide online world he calls his domain. He says the whole field is his to build and to guard. In that land a player can choose any class and any name. Each tool has a clear function, from lighting a fire to building a wall. The environment changes with the seasons on the screen. Under it all runs binary code that he does not really see. He told me the game is fun because the rules never cheat. At midnight he logs off and the room turns dark.","zh":"我表弟晚上都泡在一个他称为自己领地的广阔网络世界里。他说整片田野都归他建造和守护。在那片土地上，玩家可以任选职业和名字。每件工具都有明确的用途，从点火到砌墙。屏幕上的环境随着季节变化。而这一切底下跑着的，是他其实看不见的二进制代码。他告诉我，这游戏好玩，是因为规矩从不作弊。到半夜他下线，屋子就黑了。"},"drip":{"tw":[["drop",0],["sound",2],["filter",6],["trickle",0],["flow",2],["cistern",6],["dribble",0]],"en":"In the old farmhouse a slow drip from the tap kept us awake at night. Each drop fell into the metal sink with a clear sound. My father said the trickle came from a worn washer inside. Before breakfast he had to clean the filter and check the cistern. The water would flow again once the pipe was clear. A small dribble ran down the wall and left a dark line. He fixed it with a new ring and a twist of cloth. By noon the kitchen was dry and quiet at last.","zh":"在那座老农舍里，水龙头缓慢的滴水声让我们夜里睡不着。每一滴水落进铁水槽，都发出清脆的声响。父亲说，那细流是从里面一个磨坏的垫圈来的。早饭前他得清理过滤器，再检查水箱。管子一通畅，水就会重新流起来。一股细细的水流顺着墙淌下来，留下一道黑印。他换了个新垫圈，又用布缠了缠，把它修好了。到中午，厨房终于又干又静。"},"drown":{"tw":[["swim",0],["cover",2],["bathe",6],["overwhelm",0],["die",2],["perish",6],["submerge",0]],"en":"That autumn the river rose fast and began to drown the low fields near our village. My cousin could swim well, yet the cold water soon began to cover the small path and then to submerge the wooden bridge. We shouted at the children not to bathe in that stream, because a deep hole could overwhelm even a strong boy. One old farmer told us that a careless step could make a man perish before anyone reached him. Three sheep did die that week, and the sight stayed with me. When the rain stopped, we walked the bank and counted what the water had taken. Nobody laughed. The river had taught us its lesson.","zh":"那年秋天河水涨得很快，开始淹没我们村边的低洼田地。我表弟水性不错，可冰冷的河水很快漫过了小路，又把那座木桥淹到水下。我们朝孩子们喊，不许在那条溪里洗澡，因为一个深坑能把壮实的小伙子也吞没。一位老农说，一步不小心，人就可能在别人赶到之前死去。那一周有三只羊真的死了，那情景我一直忘不掉。雨停之后，我们沿着河岸走，清点被水冲走的东西。谁也没笑。这条河给我们上了一课。"},"endeavour":{"tw":[["try",2],["best",3],["shuttle",6],["attempt",0],["test",3],["orbit",6],["effort",0]],"en":"A young engineer joined a small team that was building a shuttle for the space agency. Their first test of the engine failed, and the second attempt was worse. The manager told them to try again, but she also asked for one honest effort each day instead of long nights. For months they would endeavour to fix a tiny valve that kept breaking. At last the shuttle reached a low orbit and stayed there for two days. The engineers said it was the best result they had ever seen. Nobody cheered loudly, because they were too tired. The old engineer wrote one line in the log: hard work is quiet.","zh":"一位年轻工程师加入了一个小团队，为航天部门造一架航天飞机。发动机的第一次测试失败了，第二次尝试更糟。经理让他们再试，但她也要求每天付出一次认真的努力，而不是熬夜。好几个月里，他们都努力去修一个总在坏的小阀门。终于，那架航天飞机进入了低轨道，并在那里待了两天。工程师们说，这是他们见过的最好的结果。没人高声欢呼，因为他们太累了。那位老工程师在日志上写了一行：辛苦的活是安静的。"},"erect":{"tw":[["raise",2],["pitch",3],["construct",2],["tall",6],["rear",0],["stalk",6],["vertical",0]],"en":"On the morning of the market, my uncle had to erect a small shelter before the sun grew hot. He would raise the poles one by one and then pitch the canvas over them. It took an hour to construct the frame and tie each corner. A tall stalk of bamboo stood at the rear as the main support. He checked that every pole was vertical before he let us hang the cloth. People walking past said the little stall looked strong. He smiled and wiped his hands on his shirt. By noon it was full of fruit, and the shade inside was cool.","zh":"赶集那天早上，我叔叔得在太阳变热之前搭起一个小棚子。他一根一根把杆子立起来，再把帆布绷上去。搭好架子、把每个角都绑牢，花了一个钟头。一根高高的竹竿立在后面，作主支撑。他先检查每根杆子是不是都竖直，才让我们挂布。路过的人说这个小摊子看着挺结实。他笑了笑，在衬衫上擦了擦手。到中午，棚里摆满了水果，底下的阴凉很凉快。"},"flicker":{"tw":[["flick",0],["flash",2],["splatter",6],["spark",0],["shine",2],["belch",6],["flutter",0]],"en":"The old lamp above the workbench began to flicker just after eight. With one flick of my hand I could make it shine again, but only for a minute. Then a blue spark jumped inside the switch and died with a small flash. A drop of oil would splatter on the floor whenever the engine belched black smoke. My father watched the flame flutter behind the glass and said nothing. He told me to wait, because a tired wire often settles by itself. So we sat in the half light and listened to the rain. In the morning he replaced the whole line.","zh":"刚过八点，工作台上方那盏旧灯就开始一闪一闪。我用手轻轻一拨，就能让它重新亮起来，可只亮一分钟。接着，开关里蹦出一个蓝色的火花，闪了一下就灭了。发动机一冒黑烟，就会有一滴油溅到地上。我父亲看着玻璃后面跳动的火苗，什么也没说。他让我等，因为累了的线路常常自己就稳下来了。于是我们坐在半明半暗里，听着雨声。第二天早上，他把整条线都换了。"},"fluid":{"tw":[["smooth",0],["gas",3],["matter",2],["surface",6],["liquid",5],["layer",6],["mobile",0]],"en":"In the school lab we had to pour a strange fluid into three different jars. The teacher said that matter can be a solid, a gas, or a liquid, and that each one behaves in its own way. Our jar held a thick liquid that moved very slowly. When we tipped it, a smooth layer formed on the surface of the glass. A young student from the mobile class next door came to watch. We could not see any gas leave the fluid, yet the weight changed a little. The teacher told us to write down every step and to keep our hands steady. Science, she said, is mostly patience.","zh":"在学校实验室里，我们得把一种奇怪的流体倒进三个不同的罐子。老师说，物质可以是固体、气体或液体，而每一种都有自己的脾性。我们的罐子里装着一种很稠的液体，动起来很慢。我们把它一歪，玻璃表面上就形成了一层光滑的膜。隔壁流动班里一个年轻学生过来看。我们看不见有任何气体从流体里跑出来，可重量却变了一点。老师让我们把每一步都记下来，手要稳。她说，科学多半就是耐心。"},"fore":{"tw":[["forward",0],["front",2],["aft",1],["starboard",6],["bow",0],["hind",6],["stem",0]],"en":"The old captain stood at the bow and pointed to the fore part of his boat. He told us that the front of a ship is the bow and the back is the aft, while the right side is called the starboard. A young sailor had to move forward along the narrow deck with a rope in his hand. The wind pushed the stem of the boat down and made the hind part lift. We held the rail and watched the grey water. The captain said a good crew never stands still. After an hour we turned back to the harbour, tired but happy.","zh":"老船长站在船头，指着船的前半部分。他告诉我们，船的前面叫 bow，后面叫 aft，右侧叫右舷。一个年轻水手得握着绳子，沿着狭窄的甲板往前走。风把船首压下去，让后半部分翘了起来。我们抓着栏杆，看着灰色的水面。船长说，好船员从不呆呆站着。一个小时后我们调头回港，累，却高兴。"},"fracture":{"tw":[["break",2],["destroy",2],["pelvis",6],["crack",2],["injure",2],["bone",6],["fault",0]],"en":"A cyclist fell on the wet road and came to the clinic with a bad fracture. The doctor looked at the picture and saw a fine crack in the bone near his pelvis. She said the fall did not destroy the joint, but it could injure the nerves if he walked too soon. For a week he had to lie still and let the bone heal. He asked whether the fault was his own, because he had taken the turn too fast. The doctor told him that a small break like his usually mends well. He promised to be more careful. Two months later he rode again, slowly.","zh":"一个骑车的人在湿滑的路上摔倒了，带着严重的骨折来到诊所。医生看着片子，发现他骨盆附近的骨头上有一条很细的裂纹。她说，这一摔并没有毁掉关节，但要是他过早走路，就可能伤到神经。有一个星期，他得静静躺着，让骨头长好。他问这过错是不是他自己的，因为他拐弯拐得太快。医生告诉他，像他这样的小裂口通常会长得很好。他保证以后更小心。两个月后，他又骑上了车，骑得很慢。"},"grease":{"tw":[["soil",0],["cover",2],["puff",6],["stain",0],["oil",2],["bake",6],["grime",0]],"en":"After a long day in the kitchen, thick grease covered every pan on the shelf. My aunt would bake bread there in the morning, so she had to clean the room first. She poured hot oil into a bowl and wiped the stove with an old cloth. A dark stain of grime had marked the wall near the window, and no soap removed it. Outside, a puff of wind blew dust from the soil through the open door. She said the work was dull but the bread was worth it. By evening the whole kitchen smelled clean. The first loaf came out golden and warm.","zh":"在厨房里忙了一整天后，架子上每个锅都糊着厚厚的油脂。我姑妈早上要在那里烤面包，所以得先把屋子收拾干净。她往碗里倒了热油，用一块旧布擦灶台。窗边墙上留下一块深色的污垢，用什么肥皂都去不掉。外面，一阵风把土里的灰尘从开着的门里吹了进来。她说这活很枯燥，但面包值得。到傍晚，整个厨房都闻着干净。头一个面包烤出来金灿灿、热腾腾的。"},"handicap":{"tw":[["check",0],["bind",3],["advantage",2],["hinder",0],["drag",3],["bias",2],["hamper",0]],"en":"A slow old computer was a real handicap for the small design team. Every morning they had to check the same files twice, and the waiting began to hinder their work. One member said the machine had become a drag on the whole office. A second problem was the bias of the manager, who trusted only the fastest workers. To hamper nobody, he agreed to share the tasks fairly. He would bind each job to a clear date, so the team could see progress. In time the new machine gave them a real advantage. The office grew quiet and quick, and people smiled again.","zh":"一台又慢又老的电脑，对这个小设计团队来说是实实在在的障碍。每天早上他们都要把同样的文件查两遍，这种等待开始拖累他们的工作。有个成员说，这台机器已经成了整个办公室的累赘。第二个问题是经理的偏见，他只信最快的员工。为了不拖累任何人，他同意公平分派任务。他把每项工作都绑定在一个明确的日期上，这样团队就能看见进展。后来新机器给了他们实实在在的优势。办公室变得安静又利落，大家又笑了。"},"hatch":{"tw":[["cover",0],["line",2],["spar",6],["brood",0],["inlay",2],["tube",6],["incubate",0]],"en":"Every spring a pair of birds would hatch three small eggs under the roof of our shed. The mother had to incubate them for many days, and she would brood without moving. My father put a wooden cover over the window so the cold wind could not reach the nest. A long spar of bamboo held the roof line straight. One morning we saw a thin tube of light and a crack in the first shell. The hatch came before noon, and three grey heads appeared. We watched them through a small inlay of glass in the door. Nobody spoke for a long time.","zh":"每年春天，都有一对鸟在我们棚屋的屋檐下孵三枚小蛋。鸟妈妈得孵上好多天，一动不动地守着。我父亲在窗户上钉了一块木板，好让冷风吹不到鸟窝。一根长竹竿把屋檐的线条撑得笔直。有天早上，我们看见一缕细细的光和第一枚蛋壳上的一道裂缝。中午之前，小雏都孵出来了，露出三个灰灰的小脑袋。我们透过门上嵌的一小块玻璃看它们。好一会儿，谁都没说话。"},"horn":{"tw":[["trumpet",0],["alarm",2],["bass",6],["trump",0],["process",2],["drum",6],["tusk",0]],"en":"In the school band my sister played a long metal horn. When she blew it, the sound was louder than the trumpet beside her. The teacher asked the drum player to keep a soft bass under the tune. For the final piece, she had to process slowly down the hall and then stop. At the end she would trump one clear note that made the whole room turn. Someone set off the fire alarm by mistake, and the practice stopped. Later she showed me a small carved tusk that her teacher kept on the shelf. It was a strange but lovely evening.","zh":"在学校乐队里，我妹妹吹一支长长的金属号。她一吹，声音比旁边的喇叭还大。老师让打鼓的人在曲子底下保持柔和的低音。到了最后一首，她得慢慢走到大厅那头，再停下来。结尾时她要吹出一个清亮的长音，让满屋子的人都转过头来。有人不小心碰响了火警铃，排练只好停下。后来她给我看老师摆在架子上的一小枚雕花獠牙。那是个奇怪却很愉快的晚上。"},"illuminate":{"tw":[["clear",0],["decorate",2],["conjure",6],["light",0],["clarify",2],["glow",6],["elucidate",0]],"en":"Before the family dinner, my uncle tried to illuminate the whole garden with small lamps. He wanted to decorate the old tree and to make each stone path clear. A weak light near the gate could barely glow in the dark. He asked me to help him and to clarify which wire went where. 'Let me elucidate,' he said, 'one line feeds all the lamps.' For a moment the scene seemed to conjure a picture from a story book. Then every lamp came on at once, and the garden was warm and bright. We stood there and forgot the cold.","zh":"家庭聚餐之前，我叔叔想用小灯把整个园子照亮。他想把老树装饰起来，让每条石子小路都看得清。门口那盏小灯昏昏暗暗，在黑暗里几乎亮不起来。他让我帮他，并说清哪根线接哪里。他说，'我来讲明白：一条线供所有灯。'有那么一瞬，这情景像是从故事书里变出来的画面。接着所有灯一下子全亮了，园子又暖又亮。我们站在那儿，把冷都忘了。"},"impulse":{"tw":[["urge",0],["drive",2],["sense",6],["momentum",0],["force",2],["disconnect",6],["pulse",0]],"en":"On the last hill of the race, a strong impulse told me to stop. I felt an urge to sit down, yet my legs kept their own momentum. The drive to finish was stronger than the pain in my chest. A doctor had once told me to check my pulse whenever the force of a climb felt too great. I had to disconnect my thoughts from the hill and count each breath instead. After a minute the sense of fear passed. I reached the top and walked the last mile home. That evening I slept like a stone.","zh":"比赛最后那道坡上，一股强烈的冲动让我想停下来。我有股坐下的欲望，可两条腿自己带着惯性往前。想跑完的那股劲，比胸口的疼更厉害。有位医生曾告诉我，只要爬坡吃力的劲头太大，就摸摸自己的脉搏。我只好把心思从这座山上断开来，改成数呼吸。过了一分钟，那种害怕的感觉过去了。我爬上了山顶，最后一段路走回了家。那天晚上我睡得像个死沉的石头。"}}});
